ZAINIUM-FSVERITY
================

zainium-fsverity is a pure-Rust library and command-line utility for working
with the Linux kernel's fs-verity subsystem. It provides a streaming user-space
Merkle tree calculator alongside safe wrappers for the Linux kernel's
<uapi/linux/fsverity.h> ioctl interfaces.


WHAT IS FS-VERITY?
------------------

fs-verity is a Linux kernel filesystem feature (supported on ext4, f2fs, and
btrfs) that makes files permanently read-only and attaches a cryptographic
Merkle tree to the inode.

Once enabled on a file:
  1. The kernel verifies every page read from disk against the Merkle tree on
     demand. Any tampered page fails with EIO before reaching user space.
  2. Applications can retrieve the file's cryptographic measurement digest in
     O(1) time via FS_IOC_MEASURE_VERITY without re-reading the file.


WHAT THIS CRATE PROVIDES
------------------------

This crate acts as a pure-Rust, zero-bloat replacement for libfsverity and
fsverity-utils, plus modern ABI compatibility enhancements:

  * Streaming User-Space Digest Engine:
    Implements the standard RustCrypto `Digest` and `std::io::Write` traits so
    build servers, package managers, and CI pipelines can compute fs-verity
    digests in chunks of any size without needing kernel or filesystem support.
    Supports SHA-256 and SHA-512.

  * Complete Linux Kernel UAPI ioctl Interface:
    - `fsverity_enable` / `fsverity_enable_config` (`FS_IOC_ENABLE_VERITY`)
    - `fsverity_measure` (`FS_IOC_MEASURE_VERITY`)
    - `fsverity_read_metadata` (`FS_IOC_READ_VERITY_METADATA`, Linux 5.12+)
    - `fsverity_is_enabled` (`FS_IOC_GETFLAGS` checking `FS_VERITY_FL`)

  * Built-in Manual Viewer:
    Includes an embedded roff renderer and fuzzy search (`fs-verity man`) that
    runs without external man-db or groff shared libraries.


KEY ARCHITECTURAL FIXES OVER UPSTREAM FS-VERITY (v0.2.0)
--------------------------------------------------------

1. Cross-Libc ioctl ABI Compatibility (glibc, musl, 32-bit, and 64-bit):
   Defines `FS_IOC_ENABLE_VERITY` (0x40806685), `FS_IOC_MEASURE_VERITY`
   (0xC0046686), `FS_IOC_READ_VERITY_METADATA` (0xC0286687), and
   `FS_IOC_GETFLAGS` as 32-bit `_IOC` bitfields cast via `as libc::Ioctl`.
   This resolves `error[E0308]: mismatched types (expected i32, found u64)` on
   musl and 32-bit targets while avoiding runtime signed-integer overflow panics
   on `_IOWR` command codes where bit 31 is set (`0xC0046686`).

2. Fixed 128-Byte `struct fsverity_enable_arg` Kernel ABI Layout:
   Upstream v0.2.0 declared `salt_ptr: *const [u8]` (a 16-byte Rust fat pointer
   on 64-bit targets), inflating the struct to 136 bytes and overwriting
   `sig_size` and `__reserved1` with `salt.len()`. Fixed to `salt_ptr: u64`
   (`__u64` in `<uapi/linux/fsverity.h>`) with a compile-time size assertion
   (`assert!(size_of::<fsverity_enable_arg>() == 128)`).

3. Fixed `struct fsverity_descriptor` Salted Hashing:
   Per Linux kernel `fs/verity/open.c` (`fsverity_hash_buffer`) and
   `Documentation/filesystems/fsverity.rst`, the zero-padded salt is prepended
   to every data and Merkle tree block, whereas the 256-byte
   `fsverity_descriptor` (which already embeds `salt_size` and `salt[32]`) is
   hashed directly without prepending the padded block salt.

4. Zero Proc-Macro Bloat:
   Removed `parse-display`, `num_enum`, and transitive `syn` / `regex-syntax`
   dependencies while keeping 100% backwards compatibility with all upstream
   types, traits, and function signatures.


COMMAND-LINE USAGE
------------------

  # Compute a user-space fs-verity digest (SHA-256 or SHA-512)
  fs-verity digest <FILE> [--alg sha256|sha512] [--block-size 4096] [--salt HEX]

  # Enable fs-verity on a file via the Linux kernel ioctl
  fs-verity enable <FILE> [--alg sha256] [--block-size 4096] [--salt HEX]

  # Measure the active fs-verity digest from the kernel in O(1) time
  fs-verity measure <FILE>

  # Check whether the FS_VERITY_FL inode flag is set on a file
  fs-verity status <FILE>

  # Dump the raw 256-byte fsverity_descriptor from the kernel
  fs-verity dump-descriptor <FILE>

  # Open the built-in manual page or fuzzy-search a topic
  fs-verity man
  fs-verity man measure


TESTING & DEVELOPMENT
---------------------

All official Linux kernel fs-verity test vectors and struct layout checks run
directly in memory via Cargo:

  cargo test --release

If you also want to generate the on-disk test files (including the 200 MB
multi-level `longfile`) to compare against the C `fsverity-utils` binary:

  python3 make_testfiles.py
  fsverity digest testfiles/*


ORIGIN & CREDITS
----------------

This project is a modernized, ABI-fixed fork of `fs-verity-rs` originally created
and written by **Ronald Volgers** (https://github.com/rvolgers/fs-verity-rs).
Enhanced and maintained by Ali Zain and Zainium Dynamics for Zainium OS and
modern Linux systems.


